coinbase-mcp-server for Debian
===============================

This package vendors its production npm dependency tree under
/usr/lib/coinbase-mcp-server, since the upstream Node.js dependency
tree (the MCP SDK, yahoo-finance2, and friends) is not available in
the Debian archive.

WARNING: when configured with live API keys this software can place
real trades and move real funds on your Coinbase account. Use
read-only or sandbox keys while evaluating it, and dry-run mode before
trading with real money.

Configure credentials via environment variables before running the
server:

  export COINBASE_API_KEY_NAME='organizations/your-org/apiKeys/your-key'
  export COINBASE_PRIVATE_KEY='-----BEGIN EC PRIVATE KEY-----...'

Configure your MCP client to run /usr/bin/coinbase-mcp-server in
stdio mode, e.g. for Claude Code (~/.claude.json):

  {
    "mcpServers": {
      "coinbase": {
        "command": "coinbase-mcp-server",
        "args": ["--stdio"],
        "env": {
          "COINBASE_API_KEY_NAME": "organizations/your-org/apiKeys/your-key",
          "COINBASE_PRIVATE_KEY": "-----BEGIN EC PRIVATE KEY-----..."
        }
      }
    }
  }

Without --stdio the server instead listens over HTTP on the port
given by $PORT (default 3000).

